From: RG EDC
Subject: [PATCH] audio/host: buffer a whole PipeWire cycle; SLOT_PERF stats

Upstream slot (GPL-3.0-or-later, https://github.com/slot-cfw/slot) paces its
emulator thread on the audio ring (push_blocking), and its host backend
opens cpal with BufferSize::Fixed(512). cpal's ALSA backend uses that as the
whole ALSA buffer (period 128). Through pipewire-alsa on a graph whose
quantum is pinned to 1280 frames (the Anbernic RG Rotate's speaker sink),
512 frames can never fill a cycle: audio is consumed at a fraction of real
time and the emulator, waiting on it, runs slow with stretched sound.

- Default the buffer to 2560 frames (two 1280-frame cycles).
  SLOT_AUDIO_BUFFER=<frames> overrides it.
- SLOT_AUDIO_DEVICE=<name> picks a cpal output device by name.
- SLOT_PERF=1 prints the chosen audio device and stream config, then once a
  second: emulated fps, render fps and frame time, audio frames consumed per
  second, ring fill, underruns and callbacks.

This patch is distributed under the same GPL-3.0-or-later licence.
---
--- a/crates/slot/src/audio/host.rs
+++ b/crates/slot/src/audio/host.rs
@@ -90,7 +90,28 @@
 
